const e={readingNotes:[{title:{zh:"算法可能供给流动性，也可能消耗它",en:"Algorithms can supply or demand liquidity"},body:{zh:"作者没有预先把算法等同于更好市场。算法可能降低提供报价的成本，也可能更快利用过时报价，使流动性提供者承担更大风险。因此，技术使用增加与价差下降同时发生，不足以单独说明是哪一种机制起作用。",en:"Algorithms may lower quoting costs or exploit stale quotes more effectively, increasing the risk faced by liquidity suppliers. The paper therefore considers competing mechanisms. Technology adoption and narrowing spreads occurring together do not by themselves identify which mechanism operates."},reference:{url:"https://faculty.haas.berkeley.edu/hender/Algo.pdf",label:{zh:"2011年期刊版 · pp. 3–4",en:"2011 journal article · pp. 3–4"}}},{title:{zh:"电子消息不等于直接识别算法",en:"Electronic messages do not directly identify algorithms"},body:{zh:"研究无法逐笔知道订单是否由计算机生成，于是用电子提交、撤单和成交报告的消息流量构造代理。这个代理也会随着同一算法更频繁撤单而变化，不只是反映采用算法的参与者增加。消息数量不能被读成算法用户数量。",en:"The study cannot directly label every order as algorithm-generated, so it uses submissions, cancellations and trade reports. The proxy can rise when existing algorithms cancel more frequently, not only when more participants adopt them. Message counts are not algorithm-user counts."},reference:{url:"https://faculty.haas.berkeley.edu/hender/Algo.pdf",label:{zh:"2011年期刊版 · §II.A",en:"2011 journal article · §II.A"}}},{title:{zh:"活动强度与流动性结果分开测量",en:"Measure activity intensity separately from liquidity outcomes"},body:{zh:"消息指标按成交额归一，目的是避免把总体交易增长全当成算法增强。流动性则用报价价差、有效价差、已实现价差与价格影响等不同指标衡量。这些结果涉及不同时间基准，不能把一个更窄的报价价差解释为所有成本都下降。",en:"Message activity is normalized by trading volume to distinguish intensity from general market growth. Liquidity outcomes include quoted, effective and realized spreads and price impact. Their reference times differ; narrower quoted spreads do not imply that every cost measure declines."},reference:{url:"https://faculty.haas.berkeley.edu/hender/Algo.pdf",label:{zh:"2011年期刊版 · §II.A–B",en:"2011 journal article · §II.A–B"}}},{title:{zh:"利用分批自动报价，而非仅比较前后趋势",en:"Use staggered autoquote introduction, not just parallel trends"},body:{zh:"NYSE在不同股票上分批引入自动报价，为作者提供算法活动变化的工具变量。识别依赖这个制度事件及相关假设，不是简单把几年间的算法增长与流动性改善相连。编辑解读：制度变化还可能有其他影响，因此需要回到原文检验识别论证。",en:"Staggered NYSE autoquote introduction supplies an instrument for algorithmic activity. Identification depends on that institutional event and its assumptions, not merely co-moving trends. Editorial interpretation: other effects of the change make the paper's identification argument essential to assess."},reference:{url:"https://faculty.haas.berkeley.edu/hender/Algo.pdf",label:{zh:"2011年期刊版 · p. 3",en:"2011 journal article · p. 3"}}},{title:{zh:"平衡面板便于比较，也带来样本边界",en:"A balanced panel aids comparison but limits the sample"},body:{zh:"样本保留整个研究期持续存在的股票，以减少样本组成变化；作者也指出这可能引入存续偏差。研究还限制股价范围，并对极端观测处理。阅读时间趋势时，应同时看到这些选择，不能把结果视为所有进入与退出公司的完整经历。",en:"Stocks present throughout the study form a balanced panel, reducing composition changes but potentially introducing survivorship effects. Price filters and treatment of extremes also shape the sample. Reported trends are not a complete history of every entering or disappearing company."},reference:{url:"https://faculty.haas.berkeley.edu/hender/Algo.pdf",label:{zh:"2011年期刊版 · §II · pp. 5–6",en:"2011 journal article · §II · pp. 5–6"}}},{title:{zh:"交易成本改善与供给者收入可以并存",en:"Lower trading costs and supplier revenues can move differently"},body:{zh:"论文报告大盘股流动性改善，同时讨论流动性提供者暂时获得更多收益的现象。更低有效价差不必意味着供给者竞争已完全消除租金。对小盘股没有显著结果也可能与工具变量较弱有关，不能据此证明算法在小盘股上完全无影响。",en:"The paper discusses improved large-stock liquidity alongside temporarily higher supplier revenues. Lower effective spreads need not imply that competition has eliminated rents. Insignificant small-stock findings may also reflect a weaker instrument, rather than proof of no effect."},reference:{url:"https://faculty.haas.berkeley.edu/hender/Algo.pdf",label:{zh:"2011年期刊版 · pp. 3–4",en:"2011 journal article · pp. 3–4"}}}],readerLimits:{zh:"研究基于2001–2005年NYSE及自动报价制度变化。消息流量是算法活动代理，不是算法账户数量；大盘股的结果不能直接推广到所有证券或今日市场。",en:"The study concerns NYSE trading in 2001–2005 and autoquote introduction. Message traffic proxies algorithmic activity, not account counts; large-stock findings do not automatically generalize to every security or today's markets."}};export{e as default};
